#: admin/settings-view.php:116
msgid ""
"<p>You have to navigate to the <a href=\"customize.php?"
"autofocus[section]=web357_customizer_section\"><strong>Customizer "
"area</strong></a> and then you will see two textareas on the left "
"sidebar. The first textarea is the \"CSS or LESS\", and the second "
"is the \"Javascript\". You can enter your CSS/LESS/JS code in these "
"input fields and you can see the result in real-time at the right "
"frame which is your frontend website.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-view.php:119
#: includes/class-w357-easy-custom-code.php:174
msgid "What is Less?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-view.php:121
#: includes/class-w357-easy-custom-code.php:175
msgid ""
"<p>In simple terms, LESS allows you to write CSS in a smarter way "
"by combining functions, mixins, operations and more. This means you "
"write more concise style information and can reuse things like "
"colors and styles more easily. The Pro edition of the Web Workbench "
"supports generating CSS files automatically rather than needing to "
"do JavaScript parsing. Read more info about less in the official "
"website lesscss.org.</p>"
msgstr ""

